{"id":"word:hebrew:H352","type":"word","title":"אַיִל","subtitle":"H352 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"properly, strength ; hence, anything strong ; specifically a chief (politically); also a ram (from his strength); a pilaster (as a strong support); an oak or other strong tree","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to אַיִל (H352) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 196 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"אַיִל (ʼayil) means properly, strength ; hence, anything strong ; specifically a chief (politically); also a ram (from his strength); a pilaster (as a strong support); an oak or other strong tree First listed occurrence: 1Chr 15 26."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"אַיִל","transliteration":"ʼayil","pronunciation":"ah'-yil","strong":"H352","lemmaId":"hebrew:H352","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["אֵילִ֤ם","אַ֧יִל","אַ֣יִל","הָ/אַ֔יִל","אֵילִ֣ם"],"morphs":[["HNcmpa",43],["HTd/Ncmsa",26],["HNcmsa",22],["HRd/Ncmsa",16],["HC/Ncmsa",16],["HNcmsc",11],["HRd/Ncmpa",8],["HC/Ncmpa",7],["HTd/Ncmpa",7],["HNcmsc/Sp3ms",6]]},"definitions":{"short":"properly, strength ; hence, anything strong ; specifically a chief (politically); also a ram (from his strength); a pilaster (as a strong support); an oak or other strong tree","usage":"mighty (man), lintel, oak, post, ram, tree.","full":"H352. ayil I. אַ֫יִל 156 noun masculine Gen 22:13 ram (as leader of flock, Late Hebrew & Aramaic id. , Assyrian ailu Dl W , Phoenician איל , = אַיִל rather than אַיָּל , compare CIS l. p. 231 ) — אַיִל (אָ֑יִל) 15:9 +; construct אֵיל Exod 29:22 +; plural אֵילִים ( אֵלִים אֵילִם, ) Gen 32:15 +; construct אֵילֵי 31:38 ; Isa 60:7 . &#8212; ram , 1 used as food Gen 31:38 (E) Deut 32:14 (compare ram of sacrifice, below e.g. Exod 29:32 compare Lev 8:31 ); as yielding wool 2Kin 3:4 ; as tribute 2Chr 17:11 ; as merchandise Ezek 27:21 ; as gift Gen 32:15 (E); in simile of leaping, skipping Psa 114:4 ( כְּא רָקְדוּ ׳הֶהָרִים ) 114:6 ; in Daniel's vision, ram with two horns symbolizing kings of Media and Persia Dan 8:3-4 , 6 , 7 (4 t. in verse); 8:20 ; figurative of rich and powerful in Israel Ezek 34:17 . 2 slain in ceremony of ratification of convenant between ׳י & Abraham Gen 15:9 (J); in Abraham's sacrifice 22:13 (twice in verse) (E); Balaam's sacrifice Num 23:1 5 t. Numbers 23 (JE); so in ritual (P), ( a ) in consecration ceremony of Aaron & his sons Exod 29:1 15 t. Exodus 29 ( מִלֻּאִים ׳א 29:22 compare 29:26 ; 29:27 ; 29:31 ) Lev 8:2 8 t. Leviticus 8 ( ׳א הַמִּלֻּאִים 8:22 ; 8:29 ׳א הָעֹלָה 8:18 ); ( b ) in guilt-offering ( אָשָׁם ) 5:15-16 , 18 ; Leviticus 5:25; 19:21-22 , compare Ezra 10:19 & ׳א הַכִּמֻּרִים Num 5:8 ; ( c ) burnt-offering ( עֹלָה ) Lev 9:2 & Num 15:6 , 11 & Ezek 46:4-5 , 6 , 7 , 11 , on day of atonement Lev 16:3 , 5 , Pentecost 23:18 ; ( d ) peace-offering ( שְׁלָמִים ) 9:4 , 18 , 19 ; beginning of month Num 28:11-12 , 14 ; compare 29:2-3 , passover 29:19 ; 29:20 compare Ezek 45:23-24 , day of firstfruits Ezekiel 45:27; Ezekiel 45:28; in 7th month 29:8 18 t. Numbers 29; ( e ) in law of Nazarite Num 6:14 , 17 , 19 ; ( f ) in consecration of altar of tabernacle 7:15 25 t. Numbers 7, compare consecration of Ezekiel's temple-altar Ezek 43:23 , 25 ; ( g ) more Generally 1Sam 15:22 ; Isa 1:11 ; Micah 6:7 ; Job 42:8 ; Psa 66:15 , also Isa 34:6 ; 60:7 ; at bringing ark to Jerusalem 1Chr 15:26 ; others occasions 29:21 ; 2Chr 13:9 ; 29:21-22 , 32 ; Ezra 8:35 ; compare figurative Jer 51:40 ; Ezek 39:18 . 3 מְאָדָּמִים אֵילִים עֹרֹת rams' skins dyed red , of covering of tabernacle Exod 25:5 ; 26:14 ; 35:7 , 23 ; 36:19 ; compare 39:34 (all P). II. אַ֫יִל noun [masculine] projecting pillar or pilaster — ׳א absolute 1Kin 6:31 (but see below) construct id. Ezek 40:14 (but strike out Co):16 (Co better אֵילָיו ); אֵיל 41:3 , אֵל 40:48 ; plural אֵילִים 40:14 +; אֵילִם 40:10 ; suffix אילו Kt 40:9 7 t.; אלו Kt 40:29 2 t. Qr (in all) אֵלָיו אֵילָיו, ; אֵלֵיהֵמָֿה 40:16 ; &#8212; pilaster or projection in wall at each side of entrance (compare Bö Proben, 302 ; NÄ 927), in Solomon's temple 1Kin 6:31 (Bö NÄ 525 reads אֵילָם ), in Ezekiel's temple Ezek 40:9-10 , 14 t. Ezekiel 40..41 + 40:14 a Ew Hi Co אילם compare ᵐ5 B; 40:38 read אילם so Sm Co compare ᵐ5 ; 40:14 b Co strike out ׳א . III. [ אַ֫יִל ?] noun masculine leader, chief (= ram, as leader of flock ? compare Di Exod 15:15 Ol §142 f Lag BN 170 & see Ezek 34:17 ) &#8212; construct אֵל 31:11 ; plural construct אֵילֵי Exod 15:15 ; Ezek 17:13 + 2Kin 24:15 Qr (Kt אולי see אוּל ); אֵלֵי Ezek 32:21 (strike out Co, see ᵐ5 ). — leader, chief ׳א מוֺאָב Exod 15:15 ; ׳א הָאָרֶץ Ezek 17:13 ; 2Kin 24:15 Qr; ׳א גּוֺיִם Ezek 31:11 ( אֵלִים Job 41:17 see below אלה ; perhaps אֵלֵיהֶם Ezek 31:14 but compare below IV. איל & also אֶל Note 1). IV. [ אַ֫יִל ?] noun masculine terebinth (probably as prominent, lofty tree, see Di Gen 12:6 ; 14:6 ) &#8212; construct אֵיל only proper name מָּארָן אֵיל see below; plural אֵילִים Isa 1:29 ; אֵלִים 57:5 construct אֵילֵי 61:3 ; suffix אֵלֵיהֶם Ezek 31:14 (&gt; strike out Co. see ᵑ8 ᵑ9 [Arabic Versions]). — terebinth (compare אֵלָה ); as marking idol-shrines Isa 1:29 ; 57:5 (so Che Di etc. &gt; gods ); figurative of ransomed ones of Zion הַצֶּדֶק אֵילֵי ; perhaps of haughty ones Ezek 31:14 .","rootNote":"from the same as 193 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 15 26","keyReferences":["1Chr 15 26","1Chr 29 21","1Kgs 6 31","1Sam 15 22","2Chr 13 9","2Chr 17 11","2Chr 29 21","2Chr 29 22"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":196,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 15 26","book":"1Chr","chapter":15,"verse":26,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אֵילִֽים","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmpa"},{"reference":"1Chr 29 21","book":"1Chr","chapter":29,"verse":21,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אֵילִ֥ים","source":"hebrew"